1
00:02:58,159 --> 00:02:59,639
Xiaotao, the station!

2
00:02:59,639 --> 00:03:00,439
Get up now!

3
00:03:00,439 --> 00:03:01,879
Li Ermiao is making a run for it!

4
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:03,159
Hurry!

5
00:03:03,159 --> 00:03:04,639
What is it? What's wrong, Auntie?

6
00:03:07,159 --> 00:03:07,759
Run!

7
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,479
You...

8
00:03:09,159 --> 00:03:11,039
You drank my liquor, didn't you?

9
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,080
Don't move!

10
00:03:18,639 --> 00:03:19,240
Screw you!

11
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:20,680
Li Ermiao!

12
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:21,479
Had a little booze,

13
00:03:21,479 --> 00:03:22,960
and forgot who you are, huh?

14
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,599
You like drinking, don't you?

15
00:03:29,039 --> 00:03:30,840
Come on, make him drink!

16
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,639
Drink it!

17
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,439
All right, that's enough.

18
00:03:47,439 --> 00:03:48,800
Stop tying him up.

19
00:03:49,439 --> 00:03:50,479
Lock the door.

20
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:52,879
Put a big lock on it.

21
00:03:52,879 --> 00:03:53,479
Got it.

22
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,240
Who's that?

23
00:04:33,279 --> 00:04:34,240
A piece of shit.

24
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,079
Isn't he your dad?

25
00:04:36,079 --> 00:04:37,360
He's a piece of shit.

26
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:38,959
Let's go, son.

27
00:04:56,079 --> 00:04:56,879
Li Ermiao.

28
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,519
As a lawyer,

29
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,759
I urge you to stay calm.

30
00:05:02,319 --> 00:05:03,560
They're evil.

31
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,319
The law will deal with the wicked,

32
00:05:05,319 --> 00:05:06,839
and they will be brought to justice.

33
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,480
You're a good person.

34
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:11,199
It was your background

35
00:05:11,199 --> 00:05:12,920
that made you suffer so much.

36
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:15,680
Don't let evil people ruin your life.

37
00:05:17,839 --> 00:05:19,000
I can't take it anymore.

38
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,519
I really can't take it.

39
00:05:22,439 --> 00:05:23,879
Then think about your family.

40
00:05:31,319 --> 00:05:33,519
I miss my mom.

41
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:57,720
Dad

42
00:11:52,679 --> 00:11:53,639
Not just me.

43
00:11:56,159 --> 00:11:57,080
You too.

44
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:31,360
Later, if they ask why you killed him,

45
00:12:32,559 --> 00:12:34,000
just tell them

46
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,600
you endured prolonged abuse.

47
00:12:40,279 --> 00:12:41,759
Under Article 260 of the Criminal Law

48
00:12:41,759 --> 00:12:42,639
on the crime of maltreatment,

49
00:12:43,399 --> 00:12:45,200
your act of killing constitutes

50
00:12:46,399 --> 00:12:47,840
an immediate act of retaliation

51
00:12:48,679 --> 00:12:50,879
carried out during or right after

52
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:52,840
unendurable prolonged abuse.

53
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,440
In judicial practice, based on

54
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,679
Article 61 of the Criminal Law

55
00:12:56,559 --> 00:12:57,559
on sentencing principles,

56
00:12:57,639 --> 00:13:01,039
and the Supreme Court's opinions

57
00:13:01,039 --> 00:13:03,960
on Balancing leniency and severity,

58
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:08,120
prolonged abuse can be taken

59
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:11,840
into consideration for sentencing.

60
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,639
I failed to help you get away.

61
00:13:16,639 --> 00:13:18,720
Nor could I stop you in time.

62
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:27,200
I'm sorry.

63
00:13:29,279 --> 00:13:30,039
I was wrong.

64
00:13:32,559 --> 00:13:33,519
I'm so sorry.

65
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,799
So pathetic.

66
00:13:41,159 --> 00:13:42,240
Actually,

67
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,840
all I wanted was a home,

68
00:13:47,759 --> 00:13:50,080
and someone who cared about me.

69
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,279
I'm not a dog.

70
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:02,159
Just... when times were hard,

71
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:04,600
if someone had shared a cigarette with me

72
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:08,360
and told me what to do,

73
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,639
maybe things would have been different.

74
00:14:32,279 --> 00:14:33,919
I'm so sorry.

75
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:44,679
I had no idea either.

76
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:49,039
I don't get it either.

77
00:14:52,639 --> 00:14:53,440
I'm sorry.

78
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,360
The doctor said

79
00:15:20,639 --> 00:15:22,279
he's currently in a state called

80
00:15:22,279 --> 00:15:24,120
spontaneous deep hypnosis,

81
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:25,399
also known as a hypnotic loop.

82
00:15:26,039 --> 00:15:27,279
A hypnotic loop...

83
00:15:28,879 --> 00:15:30,840
His brain has shut out reality.

84
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:31,960
He's locked himself away

85
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,360
in his own inner world.

86
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:35,799
His own inner world...

87
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:39,879
He got too deep into these cases lately.

88
00:15:39,879 --> 00:15:41,399
Sorting through files every day,

89
00:15:41,399 --> 00:15:43,240
interrogation transcripts and testimony.

90
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:45,519
While reviewing these cases,

91
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,279
he couldn't help but immerse himself

92
00:15:47,279 --> 00:15:48,639
in the emotions of everyone involved.

93
00:15:49,759 --> 00:15:52,120
His mind was nearly taken over by them.

94
00:15:53,399 --> 00:15:55,000
As for when he'll wake up,

95
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:57,720
it all depends on when he can break free.

96
00:16:01,159 --> 00:16:02,559
Perhaps once he comes out of it,

97
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,679
he might bring us some surprises.

98
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:09,200
Sales wants to make a pledge here:

99
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,279
We'll definitely set new records this year!

100
00:16:11,279 --> 00:16:11,960
Up by three points!

101
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:13,399
Let's all raise a glass to President Xu!

102
00:16:13,399 --> 00:16:15,919
Great! Come on, cheers!

103
00:16:16,279 --> 00:16:17,399
Alright, cheers!

104
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,440
No "President Xu" tonight.

105
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,519
We're all family here. Enjoy your food!

106
00:16:24,759 --> 00:16:25,720
Sure thing, Boss Xu!

107
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,039
Now that Sales has made their pledge,

108
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,399
Finance should make one too!

109
00:16:29,399 --> 00:16:30,480
First, a big thank-you to President Xu.

110
00:16:30,759 --> 00:16:32,039
For our company in the first half,

111
00:16:32,039 --> 00:16:33,639
there were no delays or debts, right?

112
00:16:33,639 --> 00:16:34,399
That's right!

113
00:16:34,399 --> 00:16:36,240
Here, let me propose a toast, President Xu!

114
00:16:37,159 --> 00:16:39,200
Xiaomin has performed really well lately.

115
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,240
The legal proposal she drafted—

116
00:16:41,559 --> 00:16:42,559
even President Xu praised it!

117
00:16:43,039 --> 00:16:44,720
For our company's risk assessment,

118
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:45,559
she got things off to a great start!

119
00:16:45,559 --> 00:16:46,840
Enough with the nonsense.

120
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:47,639
Right.

121
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:49,360
As if I need you to tell me!

122
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:53,679
How everyone in your company performs...

123
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:55,799
do you think I don't know?

124
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:56,960
Right, right, right.

125
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:57,759
Right.

126
00:16:57,759 --> 00:16:58,639
Come on, have a drink!

127
00:16:58,799 --> 00:16:59,759
Come on, cheers!

128
00:16:59,759 --> 00:17:00,759
Let's toast to President Xu!

129
00:17:00,759 --> 00:17:01,159
To President Xu!

130
00:17:01,159 --> 00:17:01,960
Cheers, cheers!

131
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,279
Xiaomin,

132
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:07,079
Good job.

133
00:17:07,079 --> 00:17:08,519
Thank you, President Xu. Thank you.

134
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:11,960
Sharp mind,

135
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,759
hardworking...

136
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:17,039
it's just that temper of yours...
